WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.160
What's up, gamers?

00:00:03.160 --> 00:00:11.110
A lot of SCP fans have played the free survival
horror game "SCP - Containment Breach."

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:14.949
The game's story places the player in the
shoes of a D-Class at one of the Foundation's

00:00:14.949 --> 00:00:20.850
containment sites, as they try their best
to survive a massive, catastrophic containment

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:21.850
breach.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:25.600
Many players, including some of our viewers,
feel as if the simulated experience has given

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.470
them the tools they would need to survive
a real-life containment breach.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.510
But can playing a video game really be sufficient
training for encountering some of the deadliest

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:38.109
SCPs in containment and escaping with your
life?

00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:42.199
In order to answer this question, we're going
to speculate based on one of the game's most

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:46.890
prolific players: famous YouTuber and gamer
Markiplier.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:50.749
If playing this game counts as training, then
Markiplier has enough hours logged to be a

00:00:50.749 --> 00:00:57.129
bona fide expert in facing off against the
many dangerous anomalies at the SCP Foundation.

00:00:57.129 --> 00:01:02.609
So kick back, crack open some G Fuel, and
let's see if Markiplier lives to game another

00:01:02.609 --> 00:01:03.609
day.

00:01:03.609 --> 00:01:07.530
To set the scene, let's all imagine that somehow,
through a hiccup in time and space or by some

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:13.581
sort of wish on a cursed monkey's paw, Markiplier
found himself inside of an SCP Foundation

00:01:13.581 --> 00:01:15.280
containment site.

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:19.480
That would be bad enough, but the blaring
alarms and sounds of chaos signal that he

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:24.200
arrived at the worst possible time: during
a containment breach.

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:30.100
The security systems are down, the cells are
open, and danger lurks around every corner.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:34.340
Armed with nothing but his wits and winning
personality, the only thing he can do is try

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:39.240
to navigate the facility as carefully as possible,
remember everything he's learned from his

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:45.200
time streaming the video game version of this
place, and hope he can escape with his life.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.640
Let's start with one we know he'd be well-equipped
to face: SCP-173.

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:55.820
The neck-snapping sculpture is the main antagonist
of "SCP Containment Breach," so Markiplier

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.390
would be familiar with the necessary precautions
to avoid winding up as its next victim.

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:06.070
If he happened to walk into a room and spot
the figure, frozen in his gaze, he would know

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.619
to keep his eyes on the sculpture no matter
what, and slowly back out of the room without

00:02:10.619 --> 00:02:11.619
blinking.

00:02:11.619 --> 00:02:16.390
Plus, with all of the time he spends looking
at screens, he's definitely used to keeping

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.750
his eyes on one thing for a long period of
time!

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.000
Congratulations, Mark!

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.480
You survived that one.

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.360
He's managed to get away from SCP-173 with
his neck still intact, hooray!

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.980
But as he sneaks through the hall, trying
not to draw any unwanted attention, a french-accented

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:34.319
voice breaks the silence behind him.

00:02:34.319 --> 00:02:36.330
"Good evening, my fine fellow!

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:38.250
Are you feeling quite well?"

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:44.760
There, behind him, is the SCP-049, the Plague
Doctor, in all of his beak-masked, black-robed

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:45.760
glory.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.330
"You look feverish.

00:02:47.330 --> 00:02:50.900
Please, allow me to administer some simple
tests..."

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:54.870
In this scenario, Mark would have to think
fast and use some of that patented Markiplier

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:59.660
charm to get himself out of a potentially
sticky situation before one of those gloved

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:01.209
hands can touch him.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:05.520
He would need to politely excuse himself,
insist that he just saw his doctor earlier

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:10.340
that day, and then, before the Plague Doctor
can take another step closer, run as fast

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.400
as he possibly could in the opposite direction.

00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:17.890
As Markiplier stops to catch his breath, having
thrown the Plague Doctor off of his trail,

00:03:17.890 --> 00:03:21.710
the sound of sobbing in the corner signals
that he might have just escaped the proverbial

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.780
frying pan only to wind up in the fire.

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.270
A quick cursory glance up, and the sight of
a long-limbed, pale humanoid form, would confirm

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:38.480
his suspicions: yes, indeed, he's found himself
alone with SCP-096, the Shy Guy.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.150
Remembering the details of this particular
anomaly from the game, he would look back

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:46.780
down at the ground immediately, making sure
not to glimpse the creature's face.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:52.200
As long as he avoided looking at its face,
it would stay in the corner of the room, scarcely

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:53.470
even acknowledging him.

00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:56.830
Then, he would be free to make a mad dash
for the exit.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:01.959
All the while, SCP-096 would stay hunched
over, crying, and completely unaware it was

00:04:01.959 --> 00:04:05.770
briefly in the presence of a beloved YouTube
personality.

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:09.420
Things might be going pretty well for Markiplier
so far, but uh oh!

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:11.050
What's that sound?

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:15.530
The slither of tentacles on tile, the thumping
of a large heart, and the murmuring voice

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.600
of...an elderly Englishman?

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:24.340
Poor Markiplier, video games definitely wouldn't
have prepared him for the arrival of SCP-058,

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:26.400
the Heart of Darkness.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.590
It's come out of its cage, and it's doing
just fine, but the same can't be said for

00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:35.040
any living thing that this creepy animate,
and highly hostile, creature encounters.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:41.400
"Endless suffering is the woe of ignorant
men who never lack to seek the depth of their

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:48.510
own hearts and only see the wealth of a poor
world suffering of silver and brutal gladness,"

00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:52.400
the heart whispers, as it scuttles toward
the hapless YouTuber.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:57.120
Without much prior knowledge of the anomaly,
Mark would be thoroughly unprepared for an

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:58.120
encounter with it.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:02.320
He would likely fall victim to its spiked
tentacles or the sharp stinger, and any attempt

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:07.230
to physically fight it off would be ineffective,
due to the anomaly's resilience to physical

00:05:07.230 --> 00:05:08.230
attacks.

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.650
We don't need to get into the details of how
that specifically might end.

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:13.990
It would be a bit tasteless.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:18.070
But there are friendly anomalies that Markiplier
might stumble upon too!

00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:22.540
Suppose, instead of suffering an untimely
end at the tentacles of a heart monster that

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:29.130
speaks in creepy atmospheric gibberish, he
found himself face to face with SCP-073, Cain?

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:34.080
It would be a nice reprieve, to be sure, as
Cain is generally pleasant and congenial to

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:35.930
any humans he meets.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:39.050
You never know, he might even be a fan of
Mark's work.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:43.920
The same can't be said for Cain's counterpart,
SCP-076, however.

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:48.510
It's nothing personal, Able feels murderous
rage toward any and all human beings.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:53.210
But it's hard not to take it personally when
you see Able running at you at full speed,

00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:57.430
brandishing a massive sword that's poised
to take your head off with one swing.

00:05:57.430 --> 00:06:02.680
If Markiplier faced Able on his own, he would
unfortunately not stand much of a chance.

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:07.040
Again, it's nothing personal, he's a super
powerful ancient warrior with a taste for

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.040
bloodshed.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:13.240
If Cain was in the vicinity, however, then
he might just escape unscathed.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:18.030
Cain is one of the few anomalies that can
easily oppose Able, as any damage Able manages

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:20.360
to do to him will only affect Able.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:24.669
So, the best case scenario for Mark would
be to let the two immortals go at it, while

00:06:24.669 --> 00:06:26.949
he sneaks away quietly.

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:30.860
After all the stress of navigating the containment
site, Markiplier would probably really need

00:06:30.860 --> 00:06:32.430
some cheering up.

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:36.340
After all, his entire sense of reality is
crumbling around him at a rapid pace.

00:06:36.340 --> 00:06:43.060
Good news, because SCP-999 can always sense
when someone nearby needs that frown turned

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.420
upside down.

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:48.660
The Tickle Monster doesn't appear in the Containment
Breach game, so Mark might not know what to

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:53.290
expect when he sees a large mass of bright
orange slime oozing toward him at a rapid

00:06:53.290 --> 00:06:54.290
pace.

00:06:54.290 --> 00:06:59.440
But once SCP-999 wrapped him in a big hug,
and its natural mood-boosting properties kicked

00:06:59.440 --> 00:07:04.100
in, he would know that this particular creature
is friend, not foe.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:08.229
He would give the slimy visitor some affectionate
pats, and the Tickle Monster would coo happily

00:07:08.229 --> 00:07:09.530
in return.

00:07:09.530 --> 00:07:14.669
SCP-999 might try to follow Markiplier down
the hall, but he would insist it stay where

00:07:14.669 --> 00:07:18.470
it is needed, helping the various humans and
anomalies of the Foundation when they need

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:21.440
a little bit of sweetness and light in their
lives.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.389
Then, the two would part ways, each with their
spirits lifted, and with fond memories of

00:07:26.389 --> 00:07:29.000
their new friend that would last a lifetime.

00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:34.000
But you can never let your guard down at the
SCP Foundation, not for even a second as you're

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:37.080
enjoying a hug from everyone's favorite happy
slime creature.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:42.139
If you relax and forget to keep your wits
about you, you might not notice the wall behind

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:47.620
you starting to warp and melt as something
horrible reaches through it, from a dark place

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.480
outside of space and time.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:56.199
If Markiplier turned around to find himself
face to face with the cold, dead eyes of SCP-106,

00:07:56.199 --> 00:07:58.949
The Old Man, what would happen next?

00:07:58.949 --> 00:08:03.520
The rotten Old Man appears in Containment
Breach, so Mark would know exactly how bad

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:08.310
things can get if this ominous octogenarian
gets his decaying hands on him.

00:08:08.310 --> 00:08:12.460
He would also know that doors, walls, and
other solid objects are not enough to deter

00:08:12.460 --> 00:08:16.130
this entity once he sets his sights on taking
you.

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:20.210
It's possible that Mark could run, could stay
out of the Old Man's sight until the creature

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:24.169
gets bored or finds some other, more convenient
prey to snatch up.

00:08:24.169 --> 00:08:29.320
But it's more likely that SCP-106 would be
excited by the chase, and would delight in

00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.860
the fear and pain that he is causing.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.830
Unlike in Containment Breach, where SCP-106's
movements can be predicted, the real thing

00:08:36.830 --> 00:08:39.550
is far more crafty and malicious.

00:08:39.550 --> 00:08:43.529
And there's no starting over if the Old Man
catches up to you in the real world.

00:08:43.529 --> 00:08:47.510
Unfortunately, Markiplier would likely find
himself pulled through the wall and into the

00:08:47.510 --> 00:08:51.130
entity's lair, where only doom would be waiting.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:55.860
How might Markiplier fare against another
prominent character in Containment Breach,

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.860
though?

00:08:56.860 --> 00:08:59.670
Say...one very tricky Possessive Mask?

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:05.190
Thankfully, his experience with the game would
have taught Mark in advance that SCP-035 cannot

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.510
be trusted under any circumstances.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:12.880
However, the mask in the game is at least
a little bit helpful, offering valuable information

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:17.550
about navigating the Containment Site, and
even providing insight into other threats

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:19.290
to the player's safety.

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:21.360
The real thing is nowhere near as generous.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:25.600
It has no desire to help humans, or anyone
but itself, really.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.440
If it wound up in the same room as Markiplier,
it would have one goal and one goal only:

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.130
Get him to take it out of its case, and put
it over his face.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:39.520
Hopefully, Markiplier would know better than
to wear the wicked porcelain mask, but its

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.390
psychic influence is strong.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:45.990
We couldn't blame him if he wound up succumbing
to it, putting it on and becoming the Mask's

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.260
newest human host.

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:51.320
It would be thrilled to have found such a
famous body to take over, too.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:55.850
It would pilot Markiplier out of the containment
site, take him back home, and become the first

00:09:55.850 --> 00:10:01.140
SCP with over one million YouTube subscribers
- aside from this channel, of course.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:05.380
I shudder to think what SCP-035 would do with
such a massive platform.

00:10:05.380 --> 00:10:08.550
It definitely wouldn't be anything good.

00:10:08.550 --> 00:10:11.700
Now, there aren't just anomalies at the Foundation.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:16.060
There are lots of staff members, working to
keep the well-oiled machine running smoothly.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:21.230
Of course, some are better at this than others,
and some staff are just agents of chaos all

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:22.380
on their own.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:24.760
But that makes life more fun!

00:10:24.760 --> 00:10:29.260
Imagine a team-up between the most fun-loving,
memeable researcher at the SCP Foundation

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.560
and Markiplier.

00:10:30.560 --> 00:10:33.140
That's right, Dr. Jack Bright himself.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:37.810
Now, many people don't know this, but Dr.
Bright is a big fan of gaming YouTubers, and

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:41.050
has wanted to start a channel of his own for
quite some time.

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:45.430
The Foundation won't allow him to run any
of his own social media, concerned about the

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.480
potential for secure information leaking to
the public.

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:52.390
But a chance encounter with one of his favorite
YouTuber creators would be just the kind of

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:55.430
opportunity Dr. Bright has been waiting for!

00:10:55.430 --> 00:11:00.149
Sure, Markiplier might be a bit caught off
guard by a strange man in an amulet asking

00:11:00.149 --> 00:11:04.920
him to collab, but Dr. Bright's big personality,
sense of humor, and high energy would make

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:07.550
him a great guest to have on the channel.

00:11:07.550 --> 00:11:11.400
At least until he finds something else to
distract him from his own existential dread,

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.800
and abandons his streaming dreams for that.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:17.310
He'd definitely get Markiplier to autograph
the amulet first, though.

00:11:17.310 --> 00:11:18.350
That's for sure.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:23.990
Lots of people love Markiplier, he's a congenial
guy with a passion for making enjoyable content!

00:11:23.990 --> 00:11:27.740
But there's one anomaly at the Foundation
that wouldn't like him at all.

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:33.730
In fact, it would find him, frankly, disgusssssting.

00:11:33.730 --> 00:11:38.790
But that's not his fault, SCP-682 hates all
living things.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.149
That's kind of its whole deal.

00:11:40.149 --> 00:11:42.910
Well, that, and being impossible to kill.

00:11:42.910 --> 00:11:48.270
The massive, rage-filled reptile is incredibly
dangerous to anything and anyone it encounters,

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.230
and, sadly, Markiplier would be no exception.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:56.060
This creature doesn't care about likability,
or how much a person has contributed to contemporary

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.450
internet culture.

00:11:57.450 --> 00:12:02.160
It only cares about destruction, about snapping
the poor YouTuber up in its jaws or knocking

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:06.140
him into the wall with one swish of its enormous
tail.

00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:10.390
Unless Markiplier happened to have a spare
nuclear warhead on him, it's not likely that

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:13.200
he would make it out of a meeting with SCP-682
in one piece.

00:12:13.200 --> 00:12:20.310
Oh, no, not his head- WAIT, is that the bite
of 87?!

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:27.579
Speaking of 87, how would Markiplier fare
if he stumbled upon SCP-087, The Stairwell?

00:12:27.579 --> 00:12:31.740
It's not the likeliest of events, seeing as
the doorway leading to it is constructed of

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:36.170
reinforced steel with an electro-release lock,
and disguised as the entrance to a janitor's

00:12:36.170 --> 00:12:41.610
closet in an undisclosed building, but in
this world, stranger things have happened.

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:45.180
Markiplier has played more than enough horror
games to know that finding yourself in a dark

00:12:45.180 --> 00:12:49.510
staircase that seems to go on forever, where
you can hear the distant cries of a distressed

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.570
child, isn't something anyone would ever want.

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:57.570
He could try and descend the staircase, looking
for a way out, but if he did, all that would

00:12:57.570 --> 00:13:02.709
await him is creeping dread and paranoia,
and an encounter with the frightening face

00:13:02.709 --> 00:13:05.480
of SCP-087-1.

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:09.980
His best hope in this scenario would be to
take a seat at the top of the stairs, and

00:13:09.980 --> 00:13:13.839
wait for his loyal fan base to notice he hasn't
been online for a while.

00:13:13.839 --> 00:13:18.459
The internet is a powerful thing, and it's
possible they could track him down and rescue

00:13:18.459 --> 00:13:20.700
him before things got too dire.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:24.839
Otherwise...well, best not to think about
that.

00:13:24.839 --> 00:13:28.649
Over the span of their careers, many online
personalities and digital content creators

00:13:28.649 --> 00:13:32.230
have found themselves in need of a rebrand.

00:13:32.230 --> 00:13:36.149
Maybe they decide to make a new type of creative
work, maybe they wind up at the center of

00:13:36.149 --> 00:13:41.290
a scandal, or maybe they just get bored of
doing the same thing over and over again.

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:46.200
If Markiplier ever decided to change things
up, there are dozens of ways he could go about

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:47.200
it.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:50.529
But there's one that he would need to visit
the SCP Foundation for.

00:13:50.529 --> 00:13:55.540
It wouldn't be necessarily advisable, but
what if Markiplier decided to engage in some

00:13:55.540 --> 00:14:00.640
anomalous self-improvement using SCP-914,
the Clockworks?

00:14:00.640 --> 00:14:04.850
Using live test subjects with this machine
is always a bit dicey, and he would need to

00:14:04.850 --> 00:14:08.089
be extremely careful about what setting he
used.

00:14:08.089 --> 00:14:12.149
The Very Fine setting could produce some really
exciting results.

00:14:12.149 --> 00:14:16.459
Maybe it would improve his eyesight, or give
him the ability to work long hours without

00:14:16.459 --> 00:14:18.790
experiencing creator burnout.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:23.079
Maybe it would give him the ability to fly,
or to spontaneously generate a WiFi hotspot

00:14:23.079 --> 00:14:26.960
no matter where he was, or how little phone
signal he had.

00:14:26.960 --> 00:14:29.480
Maybe it would make him the greatest gamer
in the world.

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:32.209
There's really only one reason to find out...

00:14:32.209 --> 00:14:36.710
Just make sure to hit the right button or
several million people would be very very

00:14:36.710 --> 00:14:38.089
sad.

00:14:38.089 --> 00:14:42.750
Speaking of self-improvement, what would happen
if Markiplier got his hands on an anomalous

00:14:42.750 --> 00:14:44.459
computer program?

00:14:44.459 --> 00:14:49.790
Not one of the dangerous ones, but an educational
one intended to help children learn new skills.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:55.110
SCP-5094, Miss J's Whiz Kid Schoolhouse, would
be a perfect fit.

00:14:55.110 --> 00:14:59.380
He'd have to find a way to play it on his
computer, but once he did, Markiplier could

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.290
livestream his experience with the software.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:07.920
It's uncertain how the anomalous effect of
SCP-5094 would translate to a massive audience,

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:13.300
but it would be amazing to see if thousands
of people could learn a new skill at once.

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:16.110
It wouldn't just be entertaining, it would
be potentially life-changing for everyone

00:15:16.110 --> 00:15:17.110
involved.

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:21.000
Speaking of helpful anomalies, Markiplier
would greatly benefit from an introduction

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.829
to SCP-662, the Butler's Hand Bell.

00:15:24.829 --> 00:15:29.000
Running a YouTube channel takes a ton of work,
and having an eager, supernatural assistant

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:34.480
on call 24 hours a day would probably really
improve the quality of life for everyone involved.

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:38.980
Mr. Deeds would be happy to assist with whatever
day-to-day tasks might come up, and could

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:42.079
even become a beloved background character
on the channel.

00:15:42.079 --> 00:15:46.139
Whether it's bringing Mark a bag of Taki's
or helping edit video footage, there's very

00:15:46.139 --> 00:15:49.110
little this helpful British Butler can't do!

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:53.260
When you get famous and successful, and when
you become a public figure online it seems

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:55.949
like everyone out there wants a piece of you.

00:15:55.949 --> 00:15:59.779
People want money, attention, to ride someone's
coattails to fame.

00:15:59.779 --> 00:16:04.820
But what about an anomaly that quite literally
wants a piece of Markiplier?

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:07.450
Or any person, really?

00:16:07.450 --> 00:16:12.279
SCP-082, Fernand the Cannibal, would love
to meet Markiplier, and would love to make

00:16:12.279 --> 00:16:13.930
Markiplier his meat.

00:16:13.930 --> 00:16:17.720
He would probably use his habit for lying
and spinning elaborate stories, to attempt

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.570
to entice Mark into a dangerous situation.

00:16:20.570 --> 00:16:26.670
"Hello Markiplier, it's me, your friend Jacksepticeye!"
he would say, while very visibly not being

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:27.670
who he claims to be.

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:31.790
"It's time to film a new video challenge,
see how long you can stay in the soup pot!

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:36.540
Just hop in this pot of boiling water, don't
mind me cutting up carrots and onions into

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:37.540
it..."

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:41.690
As long as Mark keeps his wits about him and
doesn't fall for the extremely obvious lies,

00:16:41.690 --> 00:16:46.430
he would likely escape this confrontation
without ending up in a YouTuber Stew.

00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:51.630
Markiplier is somewhat familiar with the layout
of the SCP Foundation containment site, thanks

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:53.620
to the gameplay of "Containment Breach."

00:16:53.620 --> 00:16:58.190
But what if, after freeing himself from one
anomalous nightmare, he stumbled into another

00:16:58.190 --> 00:16:59.920
one altogether?

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:04.559
What if, months after his inexplicable teleportation
into the containment site, after life was

00:17:04.559 --> 00:17:09.479
starting to get back to normal, he was in
the market for a brand new gaming chair?

00:17:09.479 --> 00:17:13.970
And what if he decided to prioritize convenience
and Scandinavian furniture engineering in

00:17:13.970 --> 00:17:16.269
his selection process?

00:17:16.269 --> 00:17:21.089
And what if, on top of all that, he had a
craving for some Swedish meatballs consumed

00:17:21.089 --> 00:17:22.339
in a public food court?

00:17:22.339 --> 00:17:27.039
Why, all of those factors might just lead
him to Ikea.

00:17:27.039 --> 00:17:31.190
And while there are hundreds of Ikeas around
the country, it's not impossible that he might

00:17:31.190 --> 00:17:37.049
just pick the wrong one, and find himself
lost inside of SCP-3008.

00:17:37.049 --> 00:17:41.100
Markiplier is a fairly observant guy, so it
likely wouldn't take him too long to notice

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:45.139
that something is a bit off inside of this
particular retail store.

00:17:45.139 --> 00:17:50.090
There wouldn't be any other shoppers around
him, the aisles would go on forever, and the

00:17:50.090 --> 00:17:53.389
employees inside wouldn't have faces.

00:17:53.389 --> 00:17:56.070
That last one would probably be the biggest
giveaway.

00:17:56.070 --> 00:18:00.860
Unfortunately, once someone is inside the
Infinite Ikea, it's pretty unlikely that they

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:02.590
will ever leave.

00:18:02.590 --> 00:18:06.779
He would give it a noble effort, to be sure,
exploring his surroundings and finding the

00:18:06.779 --> 00:18:10.799
best places to hide from the Ikea Staff when
the lights go out.

00:18:10.799 --> 00:18:15.479
If his phone is fully charged, he might even
be the first person to livestream from the

00:18:15.479 --> 00:18:20.090
depths of this anomalous furniture outlet,
and spread the word to his fans about the

00:18:20.090 --> 00:18:23.020
existence of SCP-3008.

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:27.590
But sadly, that stream would probably wind
up being his last, unless he somehow figured

00:18:27.590 --> 00:18:31.389
out a way to recreate his YouTube setup inside
of his strange new home.

00:18:31.389 --> 00:18:34.230
If he did, though, that would be pretty cool!

00:18:34.230 --> 00:18:37.970
Almost cool enough to make up for the fact
that he would never see any of his friends

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.389
or family ever again.

00:18:40.389 --> 00:18:44.539
Fortunately for everyone involved, it's highly
unlikely that Markiplier will end up interacting

00:18:44.539 --> 00:18:50.470
with any SCP anomalies without the safe barrier
of a computer monitor in between them.

00:18:50.470 --> 00:18:55.229
But just in case reality ever bends in on
itself and worlds begin to collide, hopefully

00:18:55.229 --> 00:18:57.690
Mark will remember everything he's learned.

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.080
And, to anyone who's ever told you otherwise:
see?

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:03.789
Playing video games can help you in the real
world!

00:19:03.789 --> 00:19:06.309
It might even save your life.

00:19:06.309 --> 00:19:12.200
Now go check out “SCP-963 What Would You
Do If You Were Immortal Like Dr. Jack Bright?”

00:19:12.200 --> 00:19:13.200
and “The Whole Story!

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:16.899
- What if SCP-096 Wore SCP-035?”

00:19:16.899 --> 00:19:18.490
for more utterly bizarre What Ifs!

